      "message": "Cool we should take this fix but now that we\u0027re on this topic, I think we discussed one issue by email where if tick is 4ms (HZ is 250), then it can cause rounding errors of upto 2ms say for a 10ms window? Especially because WALT is configurable through early_param, we wouldn\u0027t have proper control of the value. Not sure if anything better we can do here except print a message of the WALT window size at boot, or something.\n\nAlso, can you add angle brackets around the divides to not have to depend on the associativity? thanks",
